{"title":"Adding two 2-digit numbers by regrouping","key_idea":"When the ones digits add to 10 or more, regroup 10 ones into 1 ten and add the tens separately.","method":["Write the numbers one below the other, with ones in the ones place and tens in the tens place.","Add the ones digits; if the sum is 10 or more, write the ones digit below and carry 1 to the tens place.","Add the tens digits, including any carried ten, and write the result."],"worked_example":{"problem":"35 + 18 = ?","steps":["Write 35 above 18.","Add the ones: 5 + 8 = 13. Write 3 in the ones place and carry 1 ten.","Add the tens: 1 + 3 + 1 = 5. Write 5 in the tens place."],"answer":"35 + 18 = 53"},"key_terms":[{"term":"regroup","meaning":"trade 10 ones for 1 ten, or 10 tens for 1 hundred"},{"term":"carry","meaning":"move an extra ten or hundred to the next column after regrouping"}],"common_mistakes":["Forgetting to add the carried 1 to the tens column.","Writing both digits of a two-digit ones sum (like 13) instead of carrying the 1."],"remember":"If ones add to 10 or more, always carry 1 to the tens place.","quick_check":[{"q":"What is 27 + 15?","a":"27 + 15 = 42"},{"q":"What is 19 + 26?","a":"19 + 26 = 45"}],"tell_your_child":"When the ones parts make a number bigger than 9, we split off a new ten and move it to the tens column. That's called carrying, and it keeps our answer correct.","picture":{"concept_key":"c5-math-two-digit-addition-with-regrouping","scene_prompt":"A child arranging 35 single blocks and 18 single blocks into piles of ten, then counting all the tens and leftover ones together."}}
